# @boundary runs
#
# INTENT AUTHORED FROM QUICKSTART §11 ("Optional types and nil"), BEFORE RUNNING.
#
# This probe is unusual and deliberately so: it asserts the documented LIMITS as well
# as the documented behaviour. §11 does not merely say narrowing works — it names, in
# a dated note (2026-07-16), four shapes that are NOT narrowed and tells the reader to
# use `x!` for them:
#
#   - `and`-chains: "narrow only via `x!` in the 2nd operand"
#   - the `== nil` else-branch
#   - non-local receivers (`if obj.field != nil`)
#   - a block that reassigns `x`
#
# A documented limitation is a promise too, and it is the half that rots first: when
# narrowing later grows to cover an `and`-chain, the row below keeps passing (`x!` is
# always valid) while the DOC silently becomes wrong about its own restriction. So the
# rows are written so that widening narrowing cannot break them — they assert the
# workaround still works, which is what a reader following the doc will have written.
#
# What this probe canNOT see, stated rather than implied: it cannot detect that
# narrowing has grown BEYOND the doc. Only a probe asserting the un-narrowed form is
# still refused could do that, and refusing it is not something the doc promises.
def main()
    var x: int? = 42
    var z: int? = nil

    # Documented: a plain `<local> != nil` narrows the WHOLE then-block, so both a
    # bare use and arithmetic on it must compile without `!`.
    if x != nil
        print(x)
        print(x + 1)

    # Documented: "`x!` (explicit force-unwrap) also still works and is equivalent
    # here" — so the same block written the explicit way must give the same answer.
    if x != nil
        print(x!)

    # Documented NON-narrowed shape: an `and`-chain, where the doc says to reach for
    # `x!` in the second operand.
    if x != nil and x! > 40
        print("and-chain via bang")

    # Documented: the optional-unwrap binding form binds a NON-optional.
    if x as n
        print("bound ${n}")

    # Boundary: the nil value must not enter the then-block at all.
    if z != nil
        print("UNREACHABLE — a nil optional entered its own non-nil branch")
    else
        print("z is nil")
